From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <nottzaid@tutamail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:48:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] miles-bench cmdreplay: per-pool waits, live REPLAY_OFF
 switch, depth bias recorder; measured no gain

Pool operations wait only for chunks published for their own pool (plus
vkCmdExecuteCommands chunks when the pool has secondaries) instead of
everything published: guard waits on the render thread go to zero.
Feature bit 0x2000 (REPLAY_OFF) switches a pool to direct recording at
its next reset, for same-session A/B. Destroys skip the queue when the
worker is idle. vkCmdSetDepthBias2EXT is recorded. Per-function guard
wait counters.

Result (st-rp1, open world standing, VSync off, 12 ABBA pairs): replay
on 60.1 fps vs off 60.7, p95 19.6 vs 18.8 ms; circling sessions are
noise (+0.1 fps over 12 pairs). Stays off unless VKD3D_BENCH_CMD_REPLAY=1.
